    "raw": "Given:\n- Luna's food budget is 60% of her house rental budget.\n- Her phone bill budget is 10% of her food budget.\n- The total of her house rental and food budget is $240.\n\nLet's denote:\n- House rental budget as \\( R \\).\n- Food budget as \\( F \\).\n\nFrom the problem, we have:\n1. \\( F = 0.60R \\)\n2. \\( R + F = 240 \\)\n\nSubstituting \\( F \\) from the first equation into the second equation:\n\\[ R + 0.60R = 240 \\]\n\\[ 1.60R = 240 \\]\n\\[ R = \\frac{240}{1.60} \\]\n\\[ R = 150 \\]\n\nNow, using \\( R = 150 \\) to find \\( F \\):\n\\[ F = 0.60 \\times 150 \\]\n\\[ F = 90 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the phone bill budget, which is 10% of the food budget:\n\\[ \\text{Phone bill} = 0.10 \\times F \\]\n\\[ \\text{Phone bill} = 0.10 \\times 90 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Phone bill} = 9 \\]\n\nNow, we sum up all the expenses:\n\\[ \\text{Total monthly budget} = R + F + \\text{Phone bill} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total monthly budget} = 150 + 90 + 9 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total monthly budget} = 249 \\]\n\nFINAL: 249",
